<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  floppy's Reflection ability (the reference abilities/cognition/reflection) with
  its Revision (reflection/revision.py): after each turn's output it
  recalls prior episodes and the behavior inventory, asks the model to
  select at most one of bot.behavior.create, bot.behavior.change or
  bot.behavior.break, applies it, and stores the turn's CognitiveEpisode.
  The cognition (abilities/cognition/cognition.scx) invokes it as its long-lived
  child "reflection" (the original composes Reflection), with the <param>s
  database (the memory database; null: no memory) and
  model, and sends it bot.ability.reflection.input {turn,
  cognition_input, cognition_output} after each turn's output.

    idle -bot.ability.reflection.input-> recalling -> processing
      processing -bot.behavior.break-> breaking -> storing
      processing -bot.behavior.create|change-> revising { preparing ->
        authoring -> accepting | abandoning } -> storing
      processing -empty selection-> storing
    storing -> idle (bot.ability.reflection.output to the cognition)
    any failure -> failing (the episode stored, behavior null, unless
      storing failed; bot.ability.failed {message}) -> idle
    an input outside idle waits in deferred and runs from idle, in order
      (the original defers it in every busy state)

  Memory: each step that reads or writes the inventory or the episodes is
  one transaction of the memory ability (abilities/memory/memory.scx, a child per
  transaction answering bot.ability.memory.output or bot.ability.failed)
  on the database the <param> database names; the SQL lives in the <data>
  below (the original behavior/storage.py and cognition/episodes.py), SQL both
  engines (SQLite and Postgres) run: the rows come back plain and the
  datamodel assembles the episodes and behaviors from them, and a
  timestamp is UTC in the original's form, YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ. With
  database null, recalling logs <log label="reflection" expr="'absent'"> and
  answers at once.

  recalling (the original _recall_activity, _load_all_behaviors): the prior
  episodes (query_tags cognitive_episode, the turn's focus or none, oldest
  first, at most 50) and every behavior row with its triggers, any status.

  processing (the original _dispatch_select, SELECT_INSTRUCTIONS): its
  transitions for the three inventory events are the enabled transitions
  <decision:choice> reads, which <processing:collect_offered_events> tags
  with this session's id (the session that offers them, so a selection is
  sent here); <decision:pin> pins a change's and a break's name to the
  recalled inventory's names and drops both when it is empty (decision
  D100: the original offers both with any name, and a model broke
  behaviors that did not exist), and <processing:send max="1"> builds the
  original's dispatch tool with at most one event (the original's "at most
  one"), which the generate service offers as its one tool, from
  {cognition_input, cognition_output, prior_episodes, behaviors}, and
  refuses as schema-mismatch a reply that selects more. The events of
  every dispatch call it returns are each sent to this session at its
  target (#_scxml_ + target), where scxml.rs checks its data against the
  event's schema and the transition taking it applies it (the original's
  bot.ability.reflection.selected route); after them it sends itself
  bot.ability.reflection.selected, which arrives after any selection (the
  external queue is first in, first out) and goes to storing only while
  processing still waits: the empty selection. The model call is bounded by
  bot.ability.reflection.select.hop.timed_out: select_timeout_ms without
  progress once its reply streams (the first generate.progress arms it,
  each later one re-arms it; a reply that is not streamed has none) or
  select_ceiling_ms in all (decision D101).

  breaking (the original _apply_break): status BROKEN with the trimmed reason
  and status_updated_at; the row stays for a later change. An unknown
  name fails.

  revising (the original Revision): preparing stores a create's DRAFT stub
  (empty source, its triggers and description) unless the name exists,
  and loads the row (a change of an unknown name fails). authoring invokes
  the builder bot (bots/builder/builder.scx) and sends it builder.request
  with a spec built from the intent, the existing row and the turn
  (CHANGE_INSTRUCTIONS, ChangeWriteInput) and the turn behavior or
  persistent routine contract as constraints (docs/plans/
  phase5-behaviors.mdscript.md); the builder's own validate, simulate and
  no-progress loop is the original's check-and-retry. Its done is accepting: the
  document replaces the row ACTIVE (delete triggers, delete row, insert
  row, insert triggers, the original inventory.store_behavior), keeping the
  usage counters, with the original's _grounded_triggers (grounded
  before the build, so the turn behavior contract names them with this
  turn's input exactly as autonomy builds it; decision D96) and lifetime
  persistent when the document sends bot.behavior.tick, else turn. The
  request carries the original check()'s lifetime bounds (min_every_ms,
  turn_after_bound_ms), which the builder checks, and it forces a
  routine's first tick (the reference verify_apply). Its failed with the last
  draft it rejected is abandoning (the original _abandon): the row keeps that
  source as DRAFT with status_reason validation, and the turn fails with
  the original's "Reflection change abandoned: same diagnostic message after
  fix:" and the rendered diagnostics after no progress. Its failed with no
  draft (no backend, generation failures) fails the turn with no draft,
  as the original's failed change call. revising is bounded by
  inactivity (decision D101): the builder (invoked with progress_target
  '#_parent') sends builder.progress {stage} for each stage it enters, which
  disarms revising_timeout_ms, and passes on generate.progress {received}
  for each progress of its streamed generations, which arms it again, so it
  bounds a streamed
  generation that stops arriving; revising_ceiling_ms bounds the revision
  in all; the bot's bounds param may set both (bounds). When either fires, leaving revising cancels the
  revision and the turn fails with the original's "Reflection child
  cancellation timed out.".

  Reboots: the original's reflection asks for bot.reboot when a cancel does not
  finish in time or its revision asks for one. An SCXML invoke cancel is
  synchronous and the builder never asks, so this document has no reboot
  source; the cognition still forwards one from it to the body.

  storing (the original _store_activity): one CognitiveEpisode {focus,
  focus_candidates, stimulus_name, output, behavior} inserted with
  query_tags cognitive_episode, then bot.ability.reflection.output.
  Reflection alone records the turn (decision D97), so a failure after the
  recall still stores the turn's episode, with behavior null, before it
  reports bot.ability.failed; a failure of that store, or of storing
  itself, is not retried, and the failure reported is the first.

  Contracts: the events it takes reference abilities/schemas/ by
  event:schema (never inline). The builder's answer is its <donedata>,
  which scxml.rs does not check, so its conds check the shape.

  Bindings: the decision and processing namespace packages and the
  generate service package; env scopes FLOPPY_API_KEY and FLOPPY_BASE_URL to the select
  call (the builder scopes its own).
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:decision="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/decision"
       xmlns:env="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/env"
       xmlns:event="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event"
       xmlns:processing="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/processing"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="reflection" initial="idle">
  <datamodel>
    <!-- The cognition's <param>s. -->
    <data id="database" expr="null"/>
    <data id="model" expr="'Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next'"/>
    <!-- The select call's and the revision's inactivity bounds and their
         backstops (decision D101); bounds holds the bot's revising
         ones (the cognition's <param>). -->
    <data id="select_timeout_ms" expr="30000"/>
    <data id="select_ceiling_ms" expr="600000"/>
    <data id="revising_timeout_ms" expr="30000"/>
    <data id="revising_ceiling_ms" expr="1800000"/>
    <data id="bounds" expr="({})"/>
    <!-- The turn in hand (the reference InputData). -->
    <data id="turn" expr="0"/>
    <data id="cognition_input" expr="null"/>
    <data id="cognition_output" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- Recalled (the reference SelectInput). -->
    <data id="prior_episodes" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="behaviors" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- The select call. -->
    <data id="choices" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="schema" expr="null"/>
    <data id="gen_id" expr="null"/>
    <data id="selected" expr="null"/>
    <data id="gen_failure" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The dispatch call and the selection being sent (the <foreach>
         items). -->
    <data id="call" expr="null"/>
    <data id="s" expr="null"/>
    <data id="hop_timer" expr="null"/>
    <data id="ceiling_timer" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The revision's inactivity timer. -->
    <data id="revising_timer" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The applied inventory event (the original _AppliedEventData.behavior). -->
    <data id="behavior" expr="null"/>
    <!-- Revision (the reference ChangeWriteInput): the intent, whether it was a
         create, the stored row, and the builder's answer. -->
    <data id="intent" expr="null"/>
    <data id="create_intent" expr="null"/>
    <data id="existing_behavior" expr="null"/>
    <data id="write" expr="null"/>
    <data id="request" expr="null"/>
    <data id="written" expr="null"/>
    <data id="triggers" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="evidence" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="lifetime" expr="'turn'"/>
    <data id="row" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- The turn's CognitiveEpisode. -->
    <data id="episode" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The memory transaction in hand and its answer. -->
    <data id="statements" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="results" expr="null"/>
    <data id="failure" expr="null"/>
    <!-- Inputs deferred while a reflection is in hand (the reference hsm.defer). -->
    <data id="deferred" expr="[]"/>

    <!-- The original SELECT_INSTRUCTIONS, with a routine's hsm.every / hsm.at
         schedules as SCXML delayed sends. -->
    <data id="select_instructions" expr="'Select at most one offered behavior inventory event (bot.behavior.create, change, or break) when a clear repeated pattern across this turn and prior_episodes should improve future behavior, or when this turn shows a recurring or time-based need, including the user explicitly asking for something to happen on a schedule or repeatedly, that a persistent routine would serve. Otherwise return an empty selection. Use only offered events; data must match the event schema. behaviors lists installed inventory with lifetime (turn: Autonomy runs it for one matching turn; persistent: a routine that keeps running on every / at schedules, as delayed sends, across turns and restarts), status (ACTIVE|DRAFT|BROKEN), status_reason, status_updated_at, and usage: used_count / last_used_at (handled Autonomy runs) and failed_count / last_failed_at. Prefer change over break when used_count is low (not enough practice evidence). Prefer break when failures or harm outweigh practice value; include reason. create delegates a DRAFT behavior revision; change revises an existing behavior; break sets status=BROKEN (keeps inventory for later change; Autonomy will not run it and a broken routine stops); change a routine to reschedule or revise it, break it to stop it. Select intent may omit source; do not invent source here.'"/>
    <!-- The original CHANGE_INSTRUCTIONS, for the builder: the program is an
         SCXML document. -->
    <data id="change_instructions" expr="'Author or revise the SCXML program of the stored behavior. existing_behavior is the current inventory row (source may be empty for a new create stub; status may be DRAFT or BROKEN for unfinished or retired behaviors). If existing_behavior.source is empty, write a full new program from this turn, prior_episodes, and intent: invent event contracts, guards, and effects from the observed pattern only. If source is non-empty, rewrite or patch it so it better fits this turn and prior_episodes. The output is a cognition event selection object (keys: event, target?, data?, reason?) or a list of such objects, matching the shape of prior episode and this-turn outputs. Derive input fields, guards, and selection field names from the observed pattern. At runtime, fill selection data from the live input; never hardcode identifier values copied from episode examples. A turn behavior (default) answers one matching turn. When the intent or the turn calls for something recurring or time-based (or the user asked for it), write a persistent routine instead, scheduled by every or at delayed sends whose transitions send bot.behavior.tick with its selections: a persistent routine is checked by one forced tick, not the live turn, and needs no triggers.'"/>
    <data id="turn_contract" expr="'Write a turn behavior: its datamodel declares turn and input, which its invoker sets with param elements ; its invoker runs it only for a turn whose stimulus event is one of its triggers TRIGGERS, and no stimulus, event name or trigger reaches it, so it never tests one: input is the stimulus data (its fields, or {event: the data} when the data is not an object) with focus and focus_candidates added, and for this turn input is INPUT; when input holds messages and parent (a conversation\'s output), parent.data is the message this turn answers and messages is the whole conversation so far, earlier turns included, so it decides from parent.data; it sends nothing to its invoker and ends within one second in a top-level final state whose donedata content is the object {turn, handled, selected}: handled true with selected the list of selections, each naming its target, the session that receives its event, exactly as this turn\'s cognition_output names it, or handled false with selected an empty list when the behavior does not apply to this turn (never handled true with an empty list). Its tests drive no input events and expect it to finish.'"/>
    <!-- The original's persistent routine (lifetime persistent, hsm.every and
         hsm.at, behavior/schedule.py): an at schedule's occurrences are
         computed in the routine's data model by next_after (reflection.js,
         the original At.next_after), which routineContract() puts where
         NEXT_AFTER stands. -->
    <data id="routine_contract" expr="'Or, for a recurring need, write a persistent routine: it takes no params and never finishes. Each schedule is a delayed send of an event to the routine itself, armed with an id (unique in the document, so not a data id) on entry of the state that waits and cancelled on its exit, and a transition on that event back into the state that sends bot.behavior.tick to #_parent with data {name, trigger, scheduled_at, fired_at, output}, output a non-empty list of selections. every (trigger every): a fixed delay of at least 60s; scheduled_at and fired_at are both new Date().toISOString(). at (trigger at): a wall-clock time of day on chosen weekdays in one IANA time zone; declare &lt;data id=&quot;at&quot; expr=&quot;({time: \'HH:MM\', days: [\'mon\', \'tue\'], tz: \'Area/City\', rule: \'POSIX TZ rule\'})&quot;/&gt;, where days are among mon tue wed thu fri sat sun and rule is the POSIX TZ rule of tz (the last line of its zoneinfo file: EST5EDT,M3.2.0,M11.1.0 for America/New_York, CET-1CEST,M3.5.0,M10.5.0/3 for Europe/Berlin, UTC0 for UTC), and &lt;data id=&quot;next_after&quot; expr=&quot;NEXT_AFTER&quot;/&gt; exactly as given, and &lt;data id=&quot;due&quot; expr=&quot;null&quot;/&gt;; on entry assign due the value of next_after(at, Date.now()), its next occurrence {ms, iso}, before the send, whose delayexpr is (due.ms - Date.now()) + \'ms\'; scheduled_at is due.iso and fired_at new Date().toISOString(). The builder forces the first schedule\'s tick itself, so the routine\'s tests drive no input events, expect no outputs, and settle within 2000 ms.'"/>
    <!-- The original check(): ROUTINE_MIN_EVERY and TURN_SILENCE_BOUND, which
         the builder checks the document it builds against (E0009). -->
    <data id="min_every_ms" expr="60000"/>
    <data id="turn_after_bound_ms" expr="1000"/>
    <data id="no_schema_files" expr="'It is loaded from text, so it gets no schema files: any event:schema it carries is inline.'"/>

    <!-- The original episodes.episode_select_input (the 50 most recent
         episodes by created_at, then memory_id, read oldest first: its
         recent_select) and
         storage.select_all_behaviors_clauses (the behavior rows, named as
         the inventory's fields, then their triggers), each optionally for
         one name. -->
    <data id="select_episodes">SELECT content FROM (SELECT content, created_at, memory_id FROM bot_memory WHERE query_tags = 'cognitive_episode' AND content_format = 'application/json' AND (CAST(? AS TEXT) IS NULL OR context_ref IS NULL OR context_ref = ?) ORDER BY created_at DESC, memory_id DESC LIMIT 50) AS recent ORDER BY created_at, memory_id</data>
    <data id="select_behaviors">SELECT name, source, description, examples_json AS examples, lifetime, status, status_reason, status_updated_at, used_count, last_used_at, failed_count, last_failed_at FROM bot_behavior WHERE CAST(? AS TEXT) IS NULL OR name = ? ORDER BY name</data>
    <data id="select_triggers">SELECT behavior_name, "trigger" FROM bot_behavior_trigger WHERE CAST(? AS TEXT) IS NULL OR behavior_name = ? ORDER BY behavior_name, "trigger"</data>
    <!-- The original storage.mark_broken + inventory.store_behavior. -->
    <data id="break_behavior">UPDATE bot_behavior SET status = 'BROKEN', status_reason = ?, status_updated_at = replace(substr(CAST(CURRENT_TIMESTAMP AS TEXT), 1, 19), ' ', 'T') || 'Z', updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP WHERE name = ?</data>
    <!-- The original revision._draft: the create stub and its triggers, only for
         a name the recalled inventory does not hold. -->
    <data id="insert_draft">INSERT INTO bot_behavior (name, source, description, status, status_reason, status_updated_at) VALUES (?, '', ?, 'DRAFT', '', replace(substr(CAST(CURRENT_TIMESTAMP AS TEXT), 1, 19), ' ', 'T') || 'Z')</data>
    <!-- The original inventory.store_behavior (storage.replace_behavior_clauses):
         delete triggers, delete row, insert row, insert each distinct
         trigger. -->
    <data id="delete_triggers">DELETE FROM bot_behavior_trigger WHERE behavior_name = ?</data>
    <data id="delete_behavior">DELETE FROM bot_behavior WHERE name = ?</data>
    <data id="insert_behavior">INSERT INTO bot_behavior (name, source, description, examples_json, lifetime, status, status_reason, status_updated_at, used_count, last_used_at, failed_count, last_failed_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, 'ACTIVE', '', replace(substr(CAST(CURRENT_TIMESTAMP AS TEXT), 1, 19), ' ', 'T') || 'Z', ?, ?, ?, ?)</data>
    <data id="insert_trigger">INSERT INTO bot_behavior_trigger (behavior_name, "trigger") VALUES (?, ?)</data>
    <!-- The original Revision._persist_draft: the rejected source,
         storage.mark_draft(reason=validation), usage kept. -->
    <data id="draft_behavior">UPDATE bot_behavior SET source = ?, status = 'DRAFT', status_reason = 'validation', status_updated_at = replace(substr(CAST(CURRENT_TIMESTAMP AS TEXT), 1, 19), ' ', 'T') || 'Z', updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP WHERE name = ?</data>
    <!-- The original episodes.episode_insert_input; the memory id is the next
         row count as 32 zero-padded digits, since neither engine's
         randomness is unique across invocations in Wasm. -->
    <data id="insert_episode">INSERT INTO bot_memory (memory_id, scope, context_ref, subject_ref, kind, sensitivity, retention, content, content_format, query_tags) VALUES ((SELECT substr('00000000000000000000000000000000', 1, 32 - length(n)) || n FROM (SELECT CAST(COUNT(*) + 1 AS TEXT) AS n FROM bot_memory) AS c), 'memory', ?, NULL, 'task', 'standard', 'retain', ?, 'application/json', 'cognitive_episode')</data>
  </datamodel>
  <script src="reflection.js"/>

  <state id="idle">
    <transition cond="hasDeferredInput()" target="recalling">
      <assign location="turn" expr="deferred[0].turn"/>
      <assign location="cognition_input" expr="deferred[0].cognition_input"/>
      <assign location="cognition_output" expr="deferred[0].cognition_output"/>
      <assign location="deferred" expr="deferred.slice(1)"/>
      <assign location="prior_episodes" expr="[]"/>
      <assign location="behaviors" expr="[]"/>
      <assign location="behavior" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="failure" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="episode" expr="null"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.reflection.input" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.reflection.input.json"
                target="recalling">
      <assign location="turn" expr="_event.data.turn"/>
      <assign location="cognition_input" expr="_event.data.cognition_input"/>
      <assign location="cognition_output" expr="_event.data.cognition_output"/>
      <assign location="prior_episodes" expr="[]"/>
      <assign location="behaviors" expr="[]"/>
      <assign location="behavior" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="failure" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="episode" expr="null"/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <!-- The prior episodes and the whole inventory, in one transaction. -->
  <state id="recalling">
    <transition event="bot.ability.reflection.input" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.reflection.input.json">
      <assign location="deferred" expr="deferred.concat([_event.data])"/>
    </transition>
    <onentry>
      <if cond="hasNoDatabase()">
        <log label="reflection" expr="'absent'"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.reflection.output" target="#_parent"/>
      <else/>
        <assign location="results" expr="null"/>
        <assign location="statements" expr="episodeSelectStatements()"/>
        <assign location="statements" expr="behaviorSelectStatements()"/>
      </if>
    </onentry>
    <transition cond="hasNoDatabase()" target="idle"/>
    <invoke id="recalling_memory" type="scxml" src="../memory/memory.scx">
      <param name="database" expr="database"/>
      <param name="statements" expr="statements"/>
    </invoke>
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="processing">
      <assign location="prior_episodes" expr="recalledEpisodes(_event)"/>
      <assign location="behaviors" expr="recalledBehaviors(_event)"/>
      <log label="reflection" expr="recalledLog()"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.failed" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="failing">
      <assign location="failure" expr="recallFailedMessage(_event.data.message)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="error.*" target="failing">
      <assign location="failure" expr="recallFailedMessage(_event.name)"/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <!-- The select step: one structured model call over the enabled
       transitions for the inventory events. -->
  <state id="processing">
    <transition event="bot.ability.reflection.input" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.reflection.input.json">
      <assign location="deferred" expr="deferred.concat([_event.data])"/>
    </transition>
    <onentry>
      <decision:choice location="choices" events="bot.behavior.create bot.behavior.change bot.behavior.break"/>
      <processing:collect_offered_events location="choices" choices="choices"/>
      <!-- A change or a break names a behavior the inventory holds; with
           none, neither is offered (decision D100). -->
      <decision:pin location="choices" event="bot.behavior.change" property="name" values="behaviorNames()"/>
      <decision:pin location="choices" event="bot.behavior.break" property="name" values="behaviorNames()"/>
      <processing:send location="schema" choices="choices" max="1"/>
      <assign location="selected" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="gen_failure" expr="null"/>
      <!-- The inactivity bound starts with the streamed reply's first
           progress (below); until then only the backstop applies. -->
      <assign location="hop_timer" expr="'unarmed'"/>
      <send idlocation="ceiling_timer" event="bot.ability.reflection.select.hop.timed_out" delayexpr="selectCeilingDelay()"/>
    </onentry>
    <onexit>
      <cancel sendidexpr="hop_timer"/>
      <cancel sendidexpr="ceiling_timer"/>
    </onexit>
    <invoke idlocation="gen_id" type="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/services/generate"
            env:apikey="FLOPPY_API_KEY" env:baseurl="FLOPPY_BASE_URL" env:stream="FLOPPY_STREAM">
      <param name="model" expr="model"/>
      <param name="system" expr="select_instructions"/>
      <param name="prompt" expr="selectPrompt()"/>
      <param name="schema" expr="schema"/>
      <param name="schemaname" expr="'dispatch'"/>
    </invoke>
    <!-- A streamed reply's progress starts the inactivity bound, or starts
         it over (decision D101). -->
    <transition event="generate.progress" cond="isGenerate(_event)">
      <cancel sendidexpr="hop_timer"/>
      <send idlocation="hop_timer" event="bot.ability.reflection.select.hop.timed_out" delayexpr="selectTimeoutDelay()"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- The answer of this hop's call (gen_id: a late answer from an
         earlier hop's cancelled call is not this one). -->
    <transition event="generate.result" cond="isGenerate(_event)">
      <assign location="selected" expr="[]"/>
      <foreach array="_event.data.tool_calls" item="call">
        <foreach array="call.args.events" item="s">
          <log label="reflection.selected" expr="s.event"/>
          <send eventexpr="s.event" targetexpr="'#_scxml_' + s.target">
            <content expr="selectionData(s)"/>
          </send>
          <assign location="selected[selected.length]" expr="s"/>
        </foreach>
      </foreach>
      <send event="bot.ability.reflection.selected" targetexpr="'#_scxml_' + _sessionid"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="generate.failed" cond="isGenerate(_event)">
      <assign location="gen_failure" expr="generateFailure(_event)"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- The inventory events (the reference behavior_events()). -->
    <transition event="bot.behavior.create" event:schema="schemas/bot.behavior.create.json" target="revising">
      <assign location="create_intent" expr="_event.data"/>
      <assign location="intent" expr="_event.data"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.behavior.change" event:schema="schemas/bot.behavior.change.json" target="revising">
      <assign location="create_intent" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="intent" expr="_event.data"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.behavior.break" event:schema="schemas/bot.behavior.break.json" target="breaking">
      <assign location="behavior" expr="_event.data"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- After the selection, if any: none was selected. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.reflection.selected" target="storing">
      <log label="reflection.selected" expr="'none'"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="done.invoke" cond="hasSelection(_event)"/>
    <transition event="done.invoke" cond="isGenerate(_event)" target="failing">
      <assign location="failure" expr="generateFailedMessage()"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.reflection.select.hop.timed_out" cond="isSelectHopTimeout(_event)" target="failing">
      <assign location="failure" expr="selectTimedOutMessage()"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="error.*" target="failing">
      <assign location="failure" expr="selectFailedMessage(_event.name)"/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <!-- The original _apply_break: status BROKEN, the row kept. -->
  <state id="breaking">
    <transition event="bot.ability.reflection.input" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.reflection.input.json">
      <assign location="deferred" expr="deferred.concat([_event.data])"/>
    </transition>
    <onentry>
      <assign location="statements" expr="breakBehaviorStatements()"/>
    </onentry>
    <invoke id="breaking_memory" type="scxml" src="../memory/memory.scx">
      <param name="database" expr="database"/>
      <param name="statements" expr="statements"/>
    </invoke>
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json"
                cond="hasBrokenBehavior(_event)" target="storing">
      <log label="reflection.inventory" expr="brokenLog()"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="failing">
      <assign location="failure" expr="unknownBreakMessage()"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.failed" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="failing">
      <assign location="failure" expr="breakFailedMessage(_event.data.message)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="error.*" target="failing">
      <assign location="failure" expr="breakFailedMessage(_event.name)"/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <!-- The original Revision: author and check one create or change with the
       builder bot, then store the result. -->
  <state id="revising" initial="preparing">
    <transition event="bot.ability.reflection.input" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.reflection.input.json">
      <assign location="deferred" expr="deferred.concat([_event.data])"/>
    </transition>
    <onentry>
      <assign location="revising_timer" expr="'unarmed'"/>
      <send id="revising-ceiling" event="revising.after" delayexpr="revisingCeilingDelay()"/>
    </onentry>
    <onexit>
      <cancel sendidexpr="revising_timer"/>
      <cancel sendid="revising-ceiling"/>
    </onexit>
    <!-- The original's child operation bound, as one of inactivity and a
         backstop (decision D101): leaving revising cancels the revision,
         and the turn fails as the original's timing_out does. -->
    <transition event="revising.after" target="failing">
      <assign location="failure" expr="'Reflection child cancellation timed out.'"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- The builder's streamed generation made progress (the builder passes
         on its generate.progress): the inactivity bound starts, or starts
         over. A stage it enters (builder.progress) has no reply yet: the
         bound waits for that stage's first progress (decision D101). -->
    <transition event="generate.progress">
      <cancel sendidexpr="revising_timer"/>
      <send idlocation="revising_timer" event="revising.after" delayexpr="revisingTimeoutDelay()"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="builder.progress">
      <cancel sendidexpr="revising_timer"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- The original Revision._prepare: a create's DRAFT stub, then the row. -->
    <state id="preparing">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="statements" expr="[]"/>
        <if cond="isCreate()">
          <assign location="statements" expr="insertDraftStatements()"/>
          <assign location="statements" expr="insertDraftTriggersStatements()"/>
        </if>
        <assign location="statements" expr="intentBehaviorSelectStatements()"/>
      </onentry>
      <invoke id="preparing_memory" type="scxml" src="../memory/memory.scx">
        <param name="database" expr="database"/>
        <param name="statements" expr="statements"/>
      </invoke>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="authoring">
        <assign location="existing_behavior" expr="preparedBehavior(_event)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.failed" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="failing">
        <assign location="failure" expr="revisionFailedMessage(_event.data.message)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="error.*" target="failing">
        <assign location="failure" expr="revisionFailedMessage(_event.name)"/>
      </transition>
    </state>

    <!-- The builder authors, validates and simulates the program. The
         request goes once the builder has started (the next macrostep). -->
    <state id="authoring">
      <onentry>
        <if cond="isUnknownBehavior()">
          <assign location="failure" expr="unknownBehaviorMessage()"/>
          <raise event="bot.ability.reflection.revision.failed"/>
        <else/>
          <log label="reflection.revision" expr="revisionLog()"/>
          <send event="bot.ability.reflection.revision.requested"/>
        </if>
      </onentry>
      <invoke id="builder" type="scxml" src="../../bots/builder/builder.scx">
        <param name="progress_target" expr="'#_parent'"/>
      </invoke>
      <transition event="bot.ability.reflection.revision.failed" target="failing"/>
      <transition event="bot.ability.reflection.revision.requested">
        <!-- The original _grounded_triggers, before the build: the builder is
             told the triggers the behavior will be stored under. -->
        <assign location="evidence" expr="evidenceStimulusNames()"/>
        <assign location="evidence" expr="evidenceTriggerNames()"/>
        <assign location="triggers" expr="intentTriggers()"/>
        <assign location="triggers" expr="groundedTriggers()"/>
        <assign location="triggers" expr="acceptedTriggers()"/>
        <assign location="write" expr="changeWriteInput()"/>
        <assign location="write" expr="changeWriteInputWithIntent()"/>
        <assign location="request" expr="builderRequest()"/>
        <assign location="request.constraints" expr="builderConstraints()"/>
        <send event="builder.request" target="#_builder">
          <content expr="request"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="done.invoke.builder" cond="isBuilt(_event)" target="accepting">
        <assign location="written" expr="_event.data.scxml"/>
      </transition>
      <!-- The original _abandon: a failed check drafts the rejected source. -->
      <transition event="done.invoke.builder" cond="hasRejectedDraft(_event)" target="abandoning">
        <assign location="written" expr="_event.data.scxml"/>
        <assign location="failure" expr="abandonedMessage(_event)"/>
      </transition>
      <!-- The original _fail_child: a failed change call fails with no draft. -->
      <transition event="done.invoke.builder" target="failing">
        <assign location="failure" expr="builderFailedMessage(_event)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="error.*" target="failing">
        <assign location="failure" expr="revisionFailedMessage(_event.name)"/>
      </transition>
    </state>

    <!-- The original Revision._accept: the row replaced ACTIVE, usage kept, with
         the triggers authoring grounded (the original _grounded_triggers). -->
    <state id="accepting">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="lifetime" expr="writtenLifetime()"/>
        <assign location="behavior" expr="appliedBehavior()"/>
        <assign location="behavior" expr="appliedBehaviorWithSource()"/>
        <assign location="row" expr="behaviorRow()"/>
        <assign location="row" expr="behaviorRowWithUsage()"/>
        <assign location="row" expr="behaviorRowWithFailures()"/>
        <assign location="statements" expr="replaceBehaviorStatements()"/>
        <assign location="statements" expr="replaceBehaviorWithRow()"/>
        <assign location="statements" expr="replaceBehaviorWithTriggers()"/>
      </onentry>
      <invoke id="accepting_memory" type="scxml" src="../memory/memory.scx">
        <param name="database" expr="database"/>
        <param name="statements" expr="statements"/>
      </invoke>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="storing">
        <log label="reflection.inventory" expr="acceptedLog()"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.failed" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="failing">
        <assign location="failure" expr="revisionFailedMessage(_event.data.message)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="error.*" target="failing">
        <assign location="failure" expr="revisionFailedMessage(_event.name)"/>
      </transition>
    </state>

    <!-- The original Revision._abandon (_persist_draft): the row keeps the
         rejected source as DRAFT (validation), and the turn fails. -->
    <state id="abandoning">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="statements" expr="draftBehaviorStatements()"/>
      </onentry>
      <invoke id="abandoning_memory" type="scxml" src="../memory/memory.scx">
        <param name="database" expr="database"/>
        <param name="statements" expr="statements"/>
      </invoke>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="failing">
        <log label="reflection.inventory" expr="draftLog()"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.failed" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="failing"/>
      <transition event="error.*" target="failing"/>
    </state>
  </state>

  <!-- The original _store_activity: this turn's episode. -->
  <state id="storing">
    <transition event="bot.ability.reflection.input" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.reflection.input.json">
      <assign location="deferred" expr="deferred.concat([_event.data])"/>
    </transition>
    <onentry>
      <assign location="episode" expr="cognitiveEpisode(behavior)"/>
      <assign location="statements" expr="insertEpisodeStatements()"/>
    </onentry>
    <invoke id="storing_memory" type="scxml" src="../memory/memory.scx">
      <param name="database" expr="database"/>
      <param name="statements" expr="statements"/>
    </invoke>
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="idle">
      <log label="reflection.stored" expr="storedLog()"/>
      <send event="bot.ability.reflection.output" target="#_parent"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.failed" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="failing">
      <assign location="failure" expr="episodeStoreFailedMessage(_event.data.message)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="error.*" target="failing">
      <assign location="failure" expr="episodeStoreFailedMessage(_event.name)"/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <!-- The original _fail_from_stage: the failure goes to the cognition,
       after the turn's episode is stored with no behavior when storing has
       not been tried (decision D97: reflection alone records the turn). -->
  <state id="failing" initial="failing_from">
    <transition event="bot.ability.reflection.input" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.reflection.input.json">
      <assign location="deferred" expr="deferred.concat([_event.data])"/>
    </transition>
    <state id="failing_from">
      <transition cond="isEpisodeUnstored()" target="failing_storing"/>
      <transition target="failing_reported"/>
    </state>
    <state id="failing_storing">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="episode" expr="cognitiveEpisode(null)"/>
        <assign location="statements" expr="insertEpisodeStatements()"/>
      </onentry>
      <invoke id="failing_memory" type="scxml" src="../memory/memory.scx">
        <param name="database" expr="database"/>
        <param name="statements" expr="statements"/>
      </invoke>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="failing_reported">
        <log label="reflection.stored" expr="storedLog()"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.failed" event:schema="schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="failing_reported"/>
      <transition event="error.*" target="failing_reported"/>
    </state>
    <state id="failing_reported">
      <onentry>
        <log label="reflection.failed" expr="failure"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
          <param name="message" expr="failure"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
      <transition target="idle"/>
    </state>
  </state>
</scxml>
